  "measured_findings": [
    "Vulkan prefill's large backend-specific wins are GDN and long FlashAttention. At 128K Vulkan GDN is 2.711 s versus HIP 12.785 s and FlashAttention is 144.805 s versus HIP 208.121 s; Vulkan is slower in the Q4/Q5/Q8 matmul families.",
    "Decode is different: HIP's isolated decode FlashAttention template is faster than Vulkan at every measured depth (0.130/0.479/11.646 ms per token versus 0.210/0.821/12.540). Vulkan's kernel-side leads are the quantized/f32 matvec operations and lower command-buffer/fusion overhead.",
    "The Vulkan GDN shader shards each state column across lanes and uses subgroup reductions. That changes contraction order and cannot be copied under hipEngine's byte-exact recurrent-state/trajectory contract.",
    "The matched source does not support replacing hipEngine selected Q4/Q5 prefill with Vulkan MMQ: Vulkan is slower than llama.cpp HIP in both families at all three profiled prompt lengths.",
    "The production opportunity is therefore not a new hipEngine Vulkan backend. Transferable candidates are exact convolution geometry, exact HIP-side GEMV address/live-range improvements, and the common llama.cpp long-decode attention implementation; generic Vulkan dispatch/fusion ideas must be screened against hipEngine graph replay and its already-lower launch count."
  ],
